= September 2023 — The queue behind the sealed frontier

Piotr Wawrzyk, the deputy foreign minister responsible for consular affairs,
has been dismissed as prosecutors follow intermediaries, cash and expedited
applications through Polish missions abroad. Foreign Minister Zbigniew Rau
calls the system sound. PiS still campaigns as the only party able to close a
border.

At the consulates, civil servants now answer for decisions made above them;
students, workers and families with lawful applications discover that every
visa is being discussed as evidence. Lewica can follow the patronage chain,
build the lawful system PiS neglected, or borrow the government's fear of the
people to whom its officials allegedly sold access.

- @visa_inquiry
- @visa_capacity
- @visa_auction

@visa_inquiry
title: Demand an evidence-led parliamentary and prosecutor inquiry
subtitle: Keep Wawrzyk's intermediaries, contracts and chain of command at the centre; refuse an instant migration slogan.
on-arrival: border_doctrine = "Evidence-led consular accountability"; judicial_repair_mandate += 3; prosecution_oversight_capacity += 2; constitutional_restraint += 3; public_trust += 3; pis_relation -= 5; media_capacity += 2; news_headline = "The Left follows contracts, names and consular files"

Our deputies publish the contracts, consular posts and responsible officials
as a single line of inquiry. Wawrzyk becomes the beginning of the file rather
than a convenient ending, and Rau must defend who supervised the system.

The work is slower than an election slogan, but it leaves prosecutors and the
next Sejm a record that does not turn every visa holder into a suspect.

- @poland_event_queue: Put the consular file on the events desk

@visa_capacity
title: Pair the inquiry with lawful migration and consular capacity
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Give honest staff and applicants a rule-bound alternative while the right demands fewer visas of every kind.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: No policy team can turn the scandal into an administrative alternative.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; border_doctrine = "Lawful migration and consular capacity"; border_rights_standard += 5; border_security_confidence += 4; minority_safety += 3; public_trust += 2; far_right_agenda -= 2; news_headline = "A lawful border doctrine replaces the opposition's slogan auction"

Consular workers, labour inspectors and migration lawyers write one published
route for work, study and family entry, with staffing and audit duties beside
the eligibility rules. Applicants gain a system they can understand; corrupt
brokers lose the scarcity on which they traded.

PiS says we are answering corruption with more migration. We answer that a
state which knows who it admits is stronger than one which sells the stamp.

- @poland_event_queue: Send the consular alternative to the events desk

@visa_auction
title: Accuse PiS of importing the people it tells voters to fear
subtitle: Turn the government's hypocrisy into the attack; migrants already living here will pay for the premise we repeat.
on-arrival: border_doctrine = "Anti-migrant scandal competition"; border_security_confidence += 3; minority_safety -= 5; refugee_empathy -= 4; far_right_agenda += 4; left_cultural_position += 4; left_right_score += 4; social_patriot_support += 7; progressives_dissent += 8; spring_dissent += 6; razem_dissent += 7; konf_poll_momentum += 0.4; anti_ukrainian_pressure += 2; public_trust += 1; news_headline = "The opposition scandal message adopts the right's premise"

The line travels immediately: PiS frightened the country with migration while
its own officials opened a paid side door. Our social-patriotic current finally
has an attack which reaches voters outside the Left.

It reaches immigrant neighbours as well. Konfederacja need only remove the
word *corruption* and repeat the rest; progressives and Razem hear us validate
the fear before disputing who profited from it.

- @poland_event_queue: Return the migration argument to the events desk

