= September 2023 — Four questions written by one campaign

The Sejm majority orders a national referendum for 15 October, the same day as
the parliamentary election. The four questions ask about **[+
referendum_2023_questions +]**, and each is written so that the only defensible
answer is the one PiS already campaigns on. A referendum is binding at above
50% turnout; below that it is an opinion poll paid for by the state, run
through the same commissions, the same officials and the same broadcast time
that the campaign is otherwise obliged to share.

The opposition's problem is arithmetic rather than rhetoric. Refusing the
referendum ballot is lawful, it is recorded at the commission, and enough
refusals keep the result non-binding — but a party that spends the last month
teaching voters to decline a piece of paper is not spending it on why they
should vote at all.

[? if left_in_government = 1: We are inside a government that did not order
this referendum, which means our own commissioners, ministers and officials
will be asked what the state is paying for.?][? if left_in_government = 0: We
are in opposition and have no say over the wording, the funding or the
commissions. Our decision is only about what we tell our own voters to do with
the second ballot.?]

[? if nik_referral_channel = 1: Our referral channel into the Supreme Audit
Office is the one instrument in this parliament that can look at what the
referendum is costing while it is still being spent.?]
[? if nik_stance = "Resignation demanded": We spent 2019 demanding the audit
chief's resignation, and the chamber has been returning the favour by ignoring
us ever since.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "razem": Razem's organisers want the answer
argued, not avoided: the retirement-age question is ours before it is theirs.?]
[? if left_dominant_current = "social_patriot": Our social-patriotic wing warns
that telling working-class voters to refuse a ballot about the border will be
remembered longer than any tactical gain.?][? if left_dominant_current =
"spring": Wiosna's communications people want a single, clean instruction that
survives being repeated on television for four weeks.?]

- @ref23_boycott
- @ref23_answer
- @ref23_counter_questions
- @ref23_finance
- @ref23_audit

@ref23_boycott
title: Instruct our voters to refuse the referendum ballot
subtitle: Denies PiS a binding result and free campaign infrastructure; spends the closing month teaching a procedure instead of a programme.
on-arrival: referendum_2023_stance = "Organised ballot refusal"; referendum_turnout_pressure -= 12; institutional_trust += 2; ko_relation += 4; p2050_relation += 3; psl_relation += 3; pis_relation -= 6; public_trust += 1; left_poll_momentum -= 0.1; media_capacity += 1; public_mood_pending_border_security_salience += 8; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 5; news_headline = "The opposition turns ballot refusal into one common instruction"

Every democratic committee gives the same instruction and our commission
observers are briefed to record refusals correctly, because a refusal that is
not registered is simply a missing voter. The referendum falls short of the
binding threshold and the questions become what they always were: a PiS
leaflet printed at public expense.

The cost is the four weeks. Canvassers who should have been explaining wages,
housing and hospital queues spend them explaining that there are two pieces of
paper and that one of them may be declined. Turnout for the election itself
holds, but the closing argument belongs to procedure.

- @poland_event_queue: File the refusal instruction

@ref23_answer
title: Take the ballot and campaign for four honest answers
subtitle: Contests the questions on their substance and risks legitimising the exercise by helping it cross the threshold.
on-arrival: referendum_2023_stance = "Contest the questions"; referendum_turnout_pressure += 8; pension_defence_credit += 4; workers_support += 2; labor_credibility += 3; public_trust += 2; ko_relation -= 5; p2050_relation -= 3; institutional_trust -= 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.15; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_support += 10; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 10; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_backlash += 6; public_mood_pending_border_security_support -= 4; news_headline = "The Left answers the referendum instead of refusing it"

We treat the retirement-age question as an invitation rather than a trap: the
Left raised the pension age in office once and paid for it for a decade, and
saying so out loud in a national vote is worth more than a tactical silence.
The privatisation and border questions get honest answers, including the ones
that lose votes.

KO and the centre are furious. Our answers help push the referendum towards
the threshold at which it becomes binding, and the questions we did not write
are now questions we have helped legitimise.

- @poland_event_queue: Take the four answers into the campaign

@ref23_counter_questions
title: Refuse the ballot and publish four questions PiS will not ask
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Keeps the referendum non-binding while converting the last month into our own agenda.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: There is no press and field capacity left to run a parallel question campaign.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; referendum_2023_stance = "Refusal plus counter-questions"; referendum_turnout_pressure -= 9; media_capacity += 3; public_trust += 3; institutional_trust += 2; left_poll_momentum += 0.2; ko_relation += 2; workers_support += 2; health_policy_pressure += 3; household_policy_pressure += 3; public_mood_pending_social_spending_support += 6; public_mood_pending_refugee_solidarity_salience += 6; news_headline = "Refusal is paired with four questions the government refuses to ask"

Our committees decline the referendum ballot and hand out a card with four
questions of our own: waiting times, rents, minimum contracts and who owns the
energy bill. The procedure is still explained, but it is explained on the way
to something the voter recognises as their own life.

The referendum stays below the binding threshold. Our questions have no legal
force whatsoever, and we say so — which is precisely why they are quoted back
at the government for the rest of the campaign.

- @poland_event_queue: Print the counter-questions

@ref23_finance
title: Force the campaign-finance question into the electoral commission
subtitle: Attacks the state resources behind the referendum rather than the questions; a slow remedy that arrives after the votes are counted.
on-arrival: referendum_2023_stance = "Campaign-finance challenge"; referendum_turnout_pressure -= 4; party_finance_scandal += 8; pis_finance_pressure += 10; institutional_trust += 4; judicial_legitimacy += 2; public_trust += 1; pis_relation -= 5; media_capacity += 2; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 5; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_salience += 5; news_headline = "The referendum's public funding becomes an electoral-commission file"

Our lawyers file the spending: ministerial appearances, state-company
sponsorship, public-media time and government leaflets, all delivered inside
a campaign period and none of it declared against a party account. The
electoral commission cannot stop any of it before polling day.

It can examine it afterwards. The file we open this month is the one that
decides, a year from now, whether the governing party's own subsidy survives
the audit — a remedy that arrives far too late to change the count and far too
early for anyone to notice it yet.

- @poland_event_queue: Lodge the finance file

@ref23_audit
title: Refer the referendum's public spending to the audit chamber
subtitle: Requires an open referral channel. A statutory finding with document access, delivered long after the votes are counted.
choose-if: nik_referral_channel = 1
unavailable-subtitle: We have no channel into the Supreme Audit Office — that was settled in 2019 and again in January 2020.
on-arrival: referendum_2023_stance = "Audit chamber referral"; referendum_turnout_pressure -= 6; party_finance_scandal += 12; pis_finance_pressure += 14; nik_government_hostility += 8; institutional_trust += 5; public_trust += 2; media_capacity += 2; public_mood_pending_rule_of_law_support += 5; news_headline = "The audit chamber is asked what the referendum campaign is costing the state"

The referral is filed while the ministerial tours are still running: which
budget line, which state company, which public-media hour, authorised by whom.
The chamber has powers of access that no parliamentary question possesses and
no election period suspends.

It changes nothing before polling day and we say so. What it produces is a
document with a statutory author, which is a different object from an
opposition allegation and is treated differently by everybody who reads it
afterwards — including, a year from now, the electoral commission.

- @poland_event_queue: File the audit referral

